ca\nSLUG: judge-denies-kennedy-center-request-for-pause-in-ruling-ordering-trumps-name-removed-from-building\nTEXT: A US federal judge has denied the John F. Kennedy Center\'s request for a pause in a ruling ordering Donald Trump\'s name removed from the building, citing a lack of evidence to support the request. The judge made this decision after reviewing the center\'s petition, which claimed that Trump\'s name being removed would not cause significant harm to the institution. The ruling was made in response to a lawsuit filed by Trump, who claimed that the center\'s decision to remove his name was an attempt to censor him.\n\n\n',)
