etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4187005\nCREATED: 2026-06-12\nDOMAIN: apnews.com\nSLUG: congo-protest-opposition-constitution-kinshasa-f3ffbaaa242ff6dcf185ab1f54d86976\nTEXT: Violent clashes erupted in Kinshasa, Congo\'s capital, during a rally against a proposed constitutional change that opponents say could allow President Félix Tshisekedi to seek a third term. The demonstration, organized by the opposition coalition C64, was dispersed by police with tear gas after protesters clashed with pro-government supporters outside Parliament. The proposed changes, under consideration in the National Assembly, would allow the president to amend presidential term limits in the event of a "major dysfunction" that paralyzes state institutions. The Congolese Constitution bars any revision of presidential term limits, but Tshisekedi has said he would be willing to seek a third term if approved by voters in a referendum.\n\nID: 4187142\nCREATED: 2026-06-12\nDOMAIN: ctvnews.ca\nSLUG: clashes-erupt-in-congos-capital-as-opposition-rejects-changes-to-presidential-term-limits\nTEXT: Clashes have erupted in Kinshasa, the capital of the Democratic Republic of Congo, as opposition leaders reject changes to presidential term limits. The proposed changes would allow President Felix-Antoine Tshisekedi Tshilombo to serve two terms, exceeding the current limit of one term. The opposition claims the changes are an attempt to extend Tshisekedi\'s presidency indefinitely, sparking violent protests and clashes with security forces.\n\n\n',)
