etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4187722\nCREATED: 2026-06-12\nDOMAIN: petapixel.com\nSLUG: facebook-and-instagram-experiencing-widespread-outage\nTEXT: Facebook and Instagram are experiencing a widespread outage, with users reporting loading failures and error messages when attempting to search for users, view profiles, or navigate beyond the home feed on mobile devices. Many users have been unexpectedly logged out of Facebook, Messenger, and Instagram, while others are unable to log back into their accounts or access Meta\'s web services. The cause of the outage is unknown, with speculation circulating online about platform and algorithm changes or backend server issues. DownDetector reports over 100,000 outage reports for Facebook in the past half hour, with Instagram reporting 10,000.\n\nID: 4187081\nCREATED: 2026-06-12\nDOMAIN: fakti.bg\nSLUG: 1060667-a-massive-global-outage-on-meta-platforms-has-affected-millions-of-users-worldwide\nTEXT: A massive global outage on Meta platforms has affected millions of users worldwide, causing widespread disruptions. Users are unexpectedly logged out of their Facebook and Messenger accounts, with an error message appearing when they try to log back in ("An unexpected error occurred"). Those who still have access cannot refresh their feed, send messages, or load notifications. The traffic monitoring platform Downdetector is reporting a significant spike in reports of problems with Instagram as well as the desktop version of WhatsApp.\n\nID: 4187652\nCREATED: 2026-06-12\nDOMAIN: scrippsnews.com\nSLUG: facebook-instagram-users-report-widespread-outages\nTEXT: Facebook and Instagram users reported widespread outages, with issues including problems logging in, loading feeds, publishing posts, and accessing the apps and websites. Downdetector reports began declining about an hour after the outage was first reported, suggesting service was gradually being restored. Meta\'s spokesperson acknowledged the issues and stated that the company is working to resolve them.\n\nID: 4187056\nCREATED: 2026-06-12\nDOMAIN: channelnewsasia.com\nSLUG: metas-social-networks-recover-after-brief-outage-6179681\nTEXT: Meta\'s social networks, including Instagram and Facebook, recovered from a brief outage after experiencing significant issues. According to Downdetector, which tracks outages by collating status reports from multiple sources, there were over 113,000 reports of issues with Facebook and around 10,000 reports of issues with Instagram at the peak of the outage.\n\n\n',)
