etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4187474\nCREATED: 2026-06-12\nDOMAIN: deseret.com\nSLUG: utah-utes-private-equity-deal-otro-capital-finalized\nTEXT: Utah Utes Private Equity Deal Otro Capital Finalized, A Potential Model for Other Schools. \n\nUtah has completed a first-of-its-kind private equity partnership, with Otro Capital leading the deal. The partnership will centralize decision-making under the university\'s foundation, with a leadership team including Alex Schulte, former Kansas City Royals and New Orleans Saints executive, as chief commercial officer; Joel Adams, with 20 years of ticketing experience from Arizona Cardinals and LA Clippers, as chief ticketing officer; and Garrett Best, with nearly 20 years of finance experience from Mediconnect and Verisk, as chief financial officer. This model may not be the last if college athletics reform is lacking.\n\nID: 4187472\nCREATED: 2026-06-12\nDOMAIN: deseret.com\nSLUG: utah-athletics-private-equity-deal-crimson-brand-partners-otro-capital\nTEXT: The University of Utah has finalized a private equity deal with Otro Capital, a New York-based firm, to fund its athletics programs and generate additional revenue. The partnership will be led by Crimson Brand Partners, a for-profit company established to handle the commercial side of the athletic business. The university\'s president, Taylor Randall, stated that this new company will put the University of Utah at the forefront of developing creative and strategic solutions to financial challenges in college athletics.\n\n\n',)
