etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4187221\nCREATED: 2026-06-12\nDOMAIN: thedailystar.net\nSLUG: new-zealand-great-kane-williamson-retires-international-cricket-4197126\nTEXT: New Zealand great Kane Williamson retires from international cricket. Williamson made his debut in 2010 and played 378 games for New Zealand, scoring 19,346 runs with 48 centuries and six double-centuries. He averaged 54.06 in Tests, scoring 33 centuries in 110 matches. Williamson captained the side from 2016 to 2024, leading them to two World Cup finals, three semi-finals and the inaugural World Test Championship in 2021.\n\nID: 4186948\nCREATED: 2026-06-12\nDOMAIN: channelnewsasia.com\nSLUG: new-zealands-williamson-retires-internationals-after-stellar-16-year-career-6179231\nTEXT: New Zealand stalwart Kane Williamson has retired from international cricket after a 16-year career, marked by numerous accolades and leading his team to the title in the inaugural World Test Championship in 2021. Williamson, who turns 36 in August, departed mid-series in England after scoring zero and 18 runs in the opening test. He is New Zealand\'s most prolific run-scorer, with over 19,000 international runs.\n\n\n',)
