etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4187061\nCREATED: 2026-06-12\nDOMAIN: channelnewsasia.com\nSLUG: dembele-says-criticism-france-captain-mbappe-has-gone-too-far-6179741\nTEXT: France forward Ousmane Dembele has defended captain Kylian Mbappe, saying criticism of the Real Madrid striker has gone too far as France prepares for the World Cup. Dembele, a key figure for France at the tournament and contender for this year\'s Ballon d\'Or, told Spanish newspaper Marca that some commentators had overstepped in their assessment of Mbappe. Despite still being a prolific scorer, Mbappe faced criticism during Real Madrid\'s season in 2024, when the team failed to win either La Liga or the Champions League.\n\nID: 4187478\nCREATED: 2026-06-12\nDOMAIN: thestar.com.my\nSLUG: soccer-dembele-says-criticism-of-france-captain-mbappe-has-gone-too-far\nTEXT: France forward Ousmane Dembele has defended Real Madrid striker Kylian Mbappe, saying criticism of the player has become excessive as France prepares for the World Cup. Dembele, who won the Ballon d\'Or last year, believes some commentators have gone too far in their assessment of Mbappe, who remains a key figure for France despite Real\'s struggles this season. Dembele also praised coach Didier Deschamps, who will step down after the World Cup, and welcomed the idea of former France great Zinedine Zidane succeeding him.\n\n\n',)
