etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4187077\nCREATED: 2026-06-12\nDOMAIN: fakti.bg\nSLUG: 1060634-iran-will-not-give-up-control-of-the-strait-of-hormuz\nTEXT: Iran will not give up control of the Strait of Hormuz, according to a draft framework agreement between Iran and the US. The 60-day negotiation period will focus on Iran\'s nuclear program, with Tehran insisting on its "right" to enrich uranium. The draft provides for a permanent and immediate cessation of military action on all fronts, including in Lebanon. Iran\'s nuclear program will be discussed during the negotiations, with issues such as enrichment and preserved materials highlighted for inclusion in the final agreement. The project includes the release of Iranian assets worth $24 billion, with half of the amount provided even before negotiations begin.\n\nID: 4187215\nCREATED: 2026-06-12\nDOMAIN: thedailystar.net\nSLUG: iran-state-media-says-tehran-would-not-cede-control-hormuz-under-draft-us-deal-4197206\nTEXT: Iran\'s state media claims that Tehran would not cede control over the Hormuz region under a draft US deal. Final negotiations will only begin once half of Iran\'s blocked funds are released, oil sanctions are suspended, and the naval blockade is lifted. In a separate report, IRNA news agency stated that Iran would negotiate only the nuclear programme within its fundamental principles. Emphasis will be placed on issues such as Iran\'s right to enrich uranium and the retention of enriched material, which will be included in the final agreement.\n\n\n',)
